   {
    "title": "Cloud Based PTP",
    "description": "Platform: PC - Computer Communication Networking (CPE 400) - August 2013 / December 2013 - Worked with a team of two to design an application where users can go on a chat room to chat, post, and upload content. SMTP was used to send a friend request via email which consist of the requester's profile url. TCP was used for communications and content uploading. This was programmed in python. This used Tkinter for the GUI interface. This utilized Dropbox and Google Drive APIs for file utilization.\nMy role on this project:\nPrimary TCP Framework\nGUI Interface\nDropbox Functionality",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Aug 2013 - Dec 2013"
   },
   {
    "title": "Don't Get Caught",
    "description": "You are on an agent whose sole task is to try out the world most secured building filled with guards, and cameras. As you enter inside, the door closes behind you. No you must transverse to each obstacle without being caught. If you do, things will not turnout good for you. This is a 2D side scroller. This is programmed in Unity 3D. Scripts are programmed in C#. This was demoed in the UNR CSE Annual Video Game Party in December 6, 2013.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Aug 2013 - Dec 2013"
